{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Mamre.</b> The name of the plain." "<b>Kiryat ha-Arba.</b> The name of the city." "<b>Mamre, Kiryat ha-Arba.</b> To the plain of Kiryat Arba. And if you say: should it not have written מַמְרֵא הַקִּרְיַת אַרְבַּע? So is the way of Scripture with every name that is a compound — such as this one, and such as Bet Lechem, Avi Ezer, Bet El: if it becomes necessary to attach a heh to it, it places it at the head of the second word — ״בֵּית הַלַּחְמִי״ (1 Samuel 16), ״בְּעָפְרָת אֲבִי הָעֶזְרִי״ (Judges 6), ״בָּנָה חִיאֵל בֵּית הָאֱלִי״ (1 Kings 16)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:12.587532154Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}